{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms","id":1387041,"title":"Must have 3E DB Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T12:31:38-07:00","id":1387041,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Must have 3E DB Charms?","content":"What are the most useful Dragon Blooded Exalted charms in 3rd edition?<br /> <br /> I haven't read much of What Fire has Wrought, and was curious to pick the collective forum's brain on this. The terrestrial exalted essence 1 charms are probably weaker than Solar charms, but I imagine there are still several easily purchased charms that do something nifty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:45:39-07:00","id":1387048,"title":"","content":"Well firstly DBs start at Essence 2 usually so that opens up some options. Also what are you looking to do? Fight? Craft? Socialize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:06:14-07:00","id":1387054,"title":"","content":"As with every edition, Wind-Carries Words Technique is always extremely useful. Even with just Linguistics 1 and Essence 1 it's useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:42:55-07:00","id":1387084,"title":"","content":"In no particular order...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ox-Body Technique is generally good to have at least one or two purchases of by default.<br /> <br /> Wind-Carried-Words Technique, aka Glorious Terrestrial Cellphone, is one of my favorite powers in the entire Exalted canon. It's not huge, it's just a really nice utility Charm that you can use in fun ways.<br /> <br /> Elemental Concentration Trance is the gate to Elemental Bolt, but even before that it's a rather fun Charm if you like introducing facts. It lets you use various Abilities instead of Lore, which is nice if you want to introduce War or Bureaucracy or Survival facts.<br /> <br /> Elemental Bolt Attack is a cool Charm, especially if you want to hit those good good Bending notes.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Ten Thousand Dragons is an evocative, cool Integrity Charm that lets you stay true to your pals real good, and is the gate to some stuff that builds on that.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the whole Earth Awareness line is a big draw for me, because that Toph-esque tremorsense is just really cool.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Mariner Attitude is a neat Sail charm that lets you wear various social &quot;modes&quot;, sort of like Seasoned Criminal Method for Solars but more nautical. It's also the gate to Deck-Striding Prana, which lets you use Sail to boost your combat mobility. Likewise, Performance has Petal-Strewn Pavane, which uses Performance to boost combat mobility.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about must-have, but cool-to-have, definitely, depending on what you want your DB to do. One fun thing about DBs is that compared to Solars, there's a bit more in terms of Abilities reaching over to other Abilities, Charm-wise (such as the Sail and Performance mobility Charms I mentioned, a Bureaucracy Charm that enhances a specific kind of Larceny action, and others).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:50:27-07:00","id":1387086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387048#post1387048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well firstly DBs start at Essence 2 usually so that opens up some options. Also what are you looking to do? Fight? Craft? Socialize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whichever. I'm curious which charms have big bang for their buck and wide utility, with low requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:52:45-07:00","id":1387107,"title":"","content":"Well, Sorcery for DBs requires four Occult charms, so not a low requirement. However, if you are grabbing Occult anyway, even just getting TCS alone is a pretty big bang for your buck in that workings are so flexible and whatever your control is could potentially fill a big hole in your party (there seem to be quite a few spells that create long-distance flying transportation methods, for instance, one of those can be wonderfully helpful to some parties, or maybe a working could straight up justify an airship of some kind). Add summoning demons or elementals as a second spell and your versatility jumps quite a lot (esp. as more of those creatures are published).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","user":"tumbleweed664","date":". 05-09-2020, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:23:23-07:00","id":1387183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387086#post1387086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whichever. I'm curious which charms have big bang for their buck and wide utility, with low requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit hard to say generally, partly because a lot of charms are elementally themed so that they don't always mix well with other powerful charms. Notably a lot of the Essence 3 Signature charms are, as you might expect, standout awesomeness, like the Water Larceny sig that turns you bodily into water, letting her automatically escape a non-magical grapple, giving bonuses to Hardness, Evasion and Stealth rolls, which become non-charm if under water, and, of course, the ability to simply move through any obstruction that's not water tight.<br /> <br /> For stuff you can get right off the hop Virtuous Negation Defense in dodge is pretty cool, it lets you reflexively Defend Other using Evasion instead of a parry to push your ally out of the way of an attack, even out to Short range.<br /> <br /> There's Invisible Street Performer Technique in Performance which lets somebody hide in plain sight by playing music gently in the background, never to be noticed. Oh also they can play that music by picking up a tree branch and forming it into a sanxian, or causing a flower blossom to grow and stretch its petals over like a drum. They can then use that sanxian as a weapon by plucking the strings and hurling bolts of force or phantasmal beasts at her opponents.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:44:12-07:00","id":1387189,"title":"","content":"Wound-Denying Dragon Faith is a standout for me. 3 charms deep, can be taken at chargen and it essentially makes you ignore wound penalties for a scene so long as you have a fellow DB nearby, which should be always, for a low cost and, most importantly, element-agnostic. Plus the two prerequisites are far from useless on their own, and Integrity is one of those must have abilities for every character.<br /> <br /> I find it hard to justify NOT taking it on any character that is remotely combat-invested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T02:02:10-07:00","id":1387211,"title":"","content":"Of the three DB PCs in my game (Earth combat monster, Wood archer/socialite, &amp; Air socialite/sorcerer), I'm pretty sure the only Charm we all have is Ox-body Technique (and even the primary Socialite has 2 OBTs now).<br /> <br /> My personal stand-outs are:<br /> <br /> Become the Hammer (Brawl/MA Excellency, Uniform reroll 6s on damage)<br /> Force of the Mountain (Earth Dragon Style, massive bonus damage -- I use it on every attack)<br /> Earth Dragon Form (Infinite (Martial Arts) Mastery)<br /> Granite Curtain of Serenity (Integrity Excellency)<br /> Wind-Carried Words Technique (Linguistics, when regular play starts again I think we all might buy this as it's soooo good for letting the party communicate)<br /> <b>Wound Closing Touch</b> (Medicine, by the Dragons this has far and away been <u>the</u> most welcome Charm at the table -- YMMV)<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Harmonious Life-Affirming Song (Performance, who doesn't want to heal seven times faster? Some wonky book-keeping but this is an excellent combo with Wound Closing Touch. Healing Lethal from your second -2 takes 11 days* of bedrest. Or eleven hours with both these Charms. I don't mind spending a day in bed after a hard fight, but I'd rather not be down for 11 days. Plus you could go full Witcher and flurry Life-Affirming Song as you go about your daily business as normal, carrying your wounds with you and still heal over the course of a single day.)<br /> Loquacious Courtier Technique (Socialize Excellency, Mute)<br /> <br /> None of us have Dragon Mariner Attitude but I think it looks really cool. Likewise Wound-Denying Dragon Faith is high on my list to pick up.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Agree with Croakamancer below that Auspicious First-Meeting Attitude is really cool.<br /> <br /> *Mortals take 24 days (basically a month) to heal, reduced down to 2 days. If you have folks without Exalted healing, you REALLY want these Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T02:49:19-07:00","id":1387213,"title":"","content":"Auspicious First-Meeting Attitude is a really solid pick for a social character - you're always going to want to get a read on intimacies and an intimacy for you is always useful. It gets more useful if you're a traveller, or otherwise constantly meeting new people, but it's always good value","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:14:25-07:00","id":1387241,"title":"","content":"+1 on Wound Closing Touch and Auspicious First-Meeting Attitude. Friend-To-All-Nations was also really handy in the one (travel heavy) 3e game of any length I played as well, meant the social characters were pretty much always able to go all out and hit their dice caps if they needed to.<br /> <br /> Wind-Carried Words Technique scarcely needs mentioning again as it's so handy \u2013 but I'm going to. Being the team comms guy who doesn't have to use willpower is so useful in even mixed circles (was wondering if Essence may lean into effects like this for DBs given what we know).<br /> <br /> I enjoyed Stern Tutor Discipline, especially as the group I played in had strong (albeit cheerful) min-max tendencies. The rest of the group really liked being able to pretty much start at 5/5/2 in their primary attributes and burn through training times.<br /> <br /> (Same character benefitted from combo-ing Seeking Throw Technique with Stormwind Rider in fights, but that's, err niche. Same game had an Earth Dragon character with five Ox-Bodies and the aforementioned very, very good Wound-Denying Dragon Faith. They were by far the heaviest hitter in the group, although they couldn't really do anything other than fight).<br /> <br /> The Performance tree I think is really fun and versatile. Quarry Revelation Technique in Survival on someone in your group seems like kind of a must if you're going to go Wyld Hunting.<br /> <br /> Heirs adds others to the mix, but obvs not fully available yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-10-2020, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:06:52-07:00","id":1387466,"title":"","content":"Wind-Carried Words is honestly overrated - its effect is trivially replicated at basically no cost (two merit points and 1 committed mote) by a Clockword Bird. However, it is a prerequisite for Speech Without Words, an <i>awesome </i>utility power that allows you to insult people to their faces at social functions with no-one being the wiser <i>and </i>to communicate with your entire Hearth silently. The ability to say &quot;I don't trust this guy, for these specific reasons...&quot; while said guy is standing <i>right next to you </i>is invaluable.<br /> <br /> Friend-To-All-Nations is another gem, allowing you to operate at maximum dice cap anywhere, without having to blow xp on specialties. It's also a prerequisite for Seizing-the-Tongue Technique, a Charm that allows you to reroll dice on social rolls <i>after </i>you've seen the result - combined with the exploding 10s of the Presence excellency, this can give you considerable reach.<br /> <br /> I agree with the consensus that Wound-Denying Dragon Faith is great (<i>if</i> you're a team player and can reliably proc it off the back of its prerequisite, buuuuuuuut if you're not that keen on loading up with positive Intimacies towards the bunch of unstable murderhobos you're travelling with, it might easily end up as a dead Charm) and Elemental Concentration Trance is a must have (not only because there's basically no introduce fact roll you couldn't justify with it, but also because it's a prerequisite to Elemental Empowerment Meditation, the single best way you have of alleviating your teensy-tiny mote pools).<br /> <br /> Finally, while excellencies are almost always the best use of your Charm slots pre-E3, Hidden Secrets Whisper stands out even among them. It's a dice adder, so you can wring maximum value out of it even with an odd score, it gives you rerolls for free, and best of all, you can apply it to <i>so many situations</i>. Outside the wheelhouse of Occult, you can apply it to tests of speed and combat movement with a travel spell of your choice, you can use it on withering attacks with the Burning Name merit, and best of all, it gives you the cheapest and most reliable decisives of the entire Dragon-Blooded combat suite. (Admittedly, with Heirs out, Melee can finally bring its offense to par... <i>if</i> the attacker doesn't mind losing Fire Aura, has aimed on the turn before, and she's able to afford to blow 6m on top of the cost of the excellency.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:28:02-07:00","id":1387470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387466#post1387466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wind-Carried Words is honestly overrated - its effect is trivially replicated at basically no cost (two merit points and 1 committed mote) by a Clockword Bird.</div> </div> </div> </div>In WCW's defense, I would note that compared to a bird it's instant, Difficulty 5-10 to eavesdrop on assuming you even notice a message is being delivered, and cannot be destroyed, intercepted or hijacked under most circumstances. So the bird is better for everyday/trivial communication but WCW shines if privacy is a concern.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387466#post1387466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">best of all, it gives you the cheapest and most reliable decisives of the entire Dragon-Blooded combat suite. (Admittedly, with Heirs out, Melee can finally bring its offense to par... <i>if</i> the attacker doesn't mind losing Fire Aura, has aimed on the turn before, and she's able to afford to blow 6m on top of the cost of the excellency.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this cheapest and most reliable of DB decisives you speak of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-11-2020, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:42:32-07:00","id":1387521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387470#post1387470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this cheapest and most reliable of DB decisives you speak of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shooting Flight of the Brilliant Raptor or just a blast of flame with the Burning Name. In addition to however many dice you're throwing around with a full excellency, you also get to reroll up to (10s on the initial roll) failed dice. This translates to somewhere between 1.5 and 2 additional non-Charm dice on average, at no additional cost. It's basically a free Spring Follows Winter on every decisive you make, with no Aura restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:04:18-07:00","id":1387601,"title":"","content":"I agree Hidden Secrets Whisper is good, but it's not that good.<br /> <br /> 6m for 6 Charm 2 non-Charm dice is cheap.<br /> 0m for 6 Charm dice is cheaper (Stoking Bonfire Style).<br /> <br /> 2 non-Charm dice is giving a pretty reliable chance to hit, but it's not reliable damage<br /> Become the Hammer is giving you rerolls 6s. And is Uniform. And it combos easier with other effects (Cynis Ganan's Decisive cost 6m1i for +6 Charm dice, double-10s &amp; reroll 6s on damage, knock foe prone... Occult is not exactly swimming in enhancements for the Burning Name). That's far more reliable.<br /> <br /> Again, Hidden Secrets Whisper is good. But it's not setting par for Melee by a long margin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T01:36:49-07:00","id":1387664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1387601#post1387601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree Hidden Secrets Whisper is good, but it's not that good.<br /> <br /> 6m for 6 Charm 2 non-Charm dice is cheap.<br /> 0m for 6 Charm dice is cheaper (Stoking Bonfire Style).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're literally never going to get a 6m discount on Stoking Bonfire Style. Any opponent who is so far beneath you that you can proc its cost reduction <i>6 times in a row</i> will be defeated before that would happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:41:34-07:00","id":1387744,"title":"","content":"Yet another vote for Wind-Carried Words Technique. Literally every Dragon-Blood who isn't an Outcaste should be taught this within a year of exalting. In a major city, phone trees let you assemble dozens of exalts in minutes.<br /> <br /> Observer Awareness Technique is pretty great. Elemental Sheath, because Elsewhere. If you have a goon squad, Roaring Dragon Officer is going to make them WAY more effective without taking you out of the action personally.<br /> <br /> Depending on what kind of game you're in, the whole starting Occult tree could be a life-saver, or Wary Yellow Dog attitude might be a better choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:14:34-07:00","id":1388744,"title":"","content":"On a slight tangent, what are folks' thoughts for the most bang for your buck in terms for a lightly combat invested chargen DB?<br /> <br /> Came up as part of prep for a potential ease ourselves back into 3e session.<br /> <br /> Player in question is thinking physical teritary, five or less combat charms including Ox-Bodies and Excellencies, max of about 3-4 merit dots on fighty stuff and would prefer to do said fighting themselves rather than go the tyrant lizard familiar/optimised for combat DB retainer/Elemental bodyguard route. Pretty much all bonus points going into skills though, so no real issues with primary 'I kill stuff' skill being at 5 + specialty, although any dots saved for non-combat things is a bonus.<br /> <br /> Off the top of the head suggestions were the aforementioned utility Hidden Secrets Whisper with Burning Name and some Dodge; Melee with an artefact weapon and mundane armour (and maybe a mount); Dreaming Pearl; Elemental Bolt/Mantle of Elemental Power combo; or just going all out with one of the ranged skills and trusting in distance, stealth or the like.<br /> <br /> Opinion was split on wisdom of going 2/3/2 on attributes or something more unusual.<br /> <br /> Anyone used anything in that ball park they've found fun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:33:07-07:00","id":1388748,"title":"","content":"Do they know what Aspect they want to play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T13:45:30-07:00","id":1388750,"title":"","content":"A slight preference for water or air I believe (a magistrate/investigator type).<br /> <br /> That said, it's probably going to be a three to five session and wrapped up plot line to get us back up to speed with the rules before doing a proper campaign, so think they'll be pretty flexible.<br /> <br /> I'd be curious about any aspect 'packages' that have proven fun from a personal point of view too...<br /> <br /> You play a wood aspect at high essence, right? Was it high essence from the start? Fun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-15-2020, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T15:52:30-07:00","id":1388779,"title":"","content":"Raptorspam is probably the most straightforwardly powerful minimal-investment combat build (you want TCS with Flight of the Brilliant Raptor as your control spell, Threshold Warding Stance, Hopping Firecracker Evasion, annnd... you're pretty much done).<br /> <br /> You can also abuse Flying Silver Dream, which nets you an independent combatant with better than peak mortal stats and actual Solar Charms. Best bang for your buck here is probably Stoking Bonfire Style, one Ox-Body, then Arise, Moonlight Blade into Winged Argent Guardian into Flickering Lunar Protector.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, Single Point style is very powerful and engaging to play even with minimal investment and Terrestrial restrictions. You'll want Become the Hammer, one Ox-Body, then the Gathering Light Concentration + Shining Starfall Execution + SP Form triplet, and you're set. You'll never be as killy as someone who also masters Water Dragon Style and double attacks every round for free, but you'll have a set of nontrivial decisions to make in every round of every combat, which is probably more interesting than just destroying everything with Fatal Stroke Flash anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T19:09:32-07:00","id":1388820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1388750#post1388750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slight preference for water or air I believe (a magistrate/investigator type).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so as an investigator type you might want to be ready at all times, and a bit sneaky about things, so you might go thrown. Get Seeking Throw Technique, Invisibly Hidden Chakram Method and Mela's Twin Fangs, also grab Armor Rupturing Fang and two Ox-Bodies if you want to round out the charm selection. Also if you want to grab something like Speech Without Words from Linguistics that will let you roll up to the crime lair with your circle, get pat down for weapons, which will come up empty, and just when the crime lord's conversation seems to be taking a turn for the worst, signal to your crew with Speech Without Words that you're going to ambush them, also thereby entering Air Aura, then pow-pow, hit 'em with double knives right off the hop, and finish him next turn with an Armor Rupturing Fang to cripple his escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the same vein as ready at all times, a water brawler might be cool. Get 3 strength, maybe even 4 and sacrifice your dexterity to 1, and take Flotsam-and-Jetsam Approach to use improvised weapons with strength instead of dex, and also take Water Dragon's Coils to use Strength for grapple gambits as well, plus the excellency. Then get either Currents Sweep to Sea and an Ox-Body or two Ox-bodies. It should give you some nice variety to pick up any kind of improvised weapon and use it with a high attack and damage pool, and with the added bonus of being able to grapple people out to Short/Medium range with water tendrils.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to go air archery grab Flickering Candle Meditation and Hopping Firecracker Evasion, definitely don't skimp on dex. Hopping Firecracker isn't Air but who cares you're not using Aura anyway. Get the excellency for Dodge, Archery and Sky Calming Draw. Although this works a lot better if your ST remembers that penalties are a thing, especially environmental ones like slick ground, rain, wind, darkness, dust storms, fog, snow, etc. Since the dodge and archery charms do a lot of penalty negation which your enemies won't get. You won't need ox-bodies as much here since as soon as you escape to Short range the rest of your circle will keep most enemies trapped and thus safely away from you. Although I might pick up one later.<br /> <br /> <br /> You could also grab almost any of the Immaculate Dragon styles and you should be pretty good, although maybe avoid Fire Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T02:09:50-07:00","id":1388869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1387041-must-have-3e-db-charms?p=1388750#post1388750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You play a wood aspect at high essence, right? Was it high essence from the start? Fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 4. It was a replacement for my Zenith whom I retired. I'm enjoying Osiris so far, but it's a low combat game and I haven't played him that long, so I don't have a lot of examples about how good/fun he is in combat.<br /> My build is essentially a few Archery charms, lots of ox-bodies, and some anti-Undead charms (which Wood is good at, also I have an artefact bow with an anti-CoD evocation), as Undead frequently feature in that game.<br /> <br /> If you want a really low investment, I'd generally recommend Melee or Brawl, because you can take 5 dots for 2 freebies if you favour it and have a good Defence, rather than having to also buy Dodge. Of course, if it's Air aspected, then a Thrown build where you stand further away is fine as you get attacked less (assuming the other PCs are front-line fighters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T19:10:26-07:00","id":1389160,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go against the grain and say the Mute Excellencies are the best DB charms if you are doing those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T04:18:07-07:00","id":1390746,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all for all the input, went with something very akin to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>'s brawler as we were both interested in seeing how Dex 1 might work (answer: lots of fun, but boy do you miss Dex for things like rising from prone and passive defence. Player really liked him though).<br /> <br /> I'll maybe stick the final fight (DB magistrate being jumped by 4 bravos armed with different weapons) from the session in the Arena when I get a sec as I took notes. We explicitly tried to use weapon tags and gambits as much as possible (they ended up short-shrifted apart from grapples and balanced in our previous game and we wanted to play around with them a bit more), wondered a while back if that might offer up some discussion points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-22-2020, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}